# Raw downloaded data is reproducible via src/ingest/ — never commit it
data/raw/

# Tabular staging layer of the public data dump (rebuilt by src/ingest/public_dump/); the tracked
# manifest and coverage summaries live in data/studies/public_data_dump/
data/dump/

# Large downloaded audit evidence stays local; keep scripts, receipts and summaries.
data/studies/tennis_data_audit/polymarket/raw/
data/studies/tennis_data_audit/polymarket/events.jsonl
data/studies/tennis_data_audit/polymarket/markets.jsonl.gz
data/studies/tennis_data_audit/public/raw/

# Large generated audit outputs stay local; rerun the named script over the ignored inputs above.
# Their summaries (polymarket_public_link_summary.json, table_audit.json) stay tracked.
#   link_public_results_to_polymarket.py -> candidate links (16 MB), unmatched records (6 MB)
#   audit_public_tables.py               -> Open Tennis Data quarantine records (1 MB)
data/studies/tennis_data_audit/public/polymarket_public_candidate_links.json
data/studies/tennis_data_audit/public/polymarket_public_unmatched.json
data/studies/tennis_data_audit/public/open_tennis_quarantine_records.json

# The data map's cache of slow-source summaries (rebuilt by src/eda/data_map/measure.py --refresh)
data/studies/data_map/_cache/

# Parquet here is always a staged or derived table rebuilt by scripts, and a DuckDB file would be
# rebuilt from Parquet. Keep hand-curated tables as CSV or YAML so they stay tracked.
*.parquet
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# Arrays and model state are always written by a script: model fits, IOS runs, solver caches, profile arrays,
# TabPFN executor states (3.6 GB each) and model weights. Their readings are kept in the tracked JSON and CSV
# records beside them; rebuild with the script that wrote them. The .npz files git tracked before 14 Oct 2026
# stay tracked until taken out of the index (data/LARGE_FILES.md, "Already tracked").
*.npz
*.joblib
*.safetensors
# The daily engine's temporary solver caches (about 2.5 GB each), written into a run or checkpoint folder and
# deleted when their step ends (src/eda/daily_prediction/dp_state.py); named in case the rule above is narrowed
_ios_cache_*.npz
_cache_tmp.npz
# A candidate Stage 0's left-out rows (25-31 MB each), written again with the candidate by
# src/eda/lower_level_evidence/candidate_stage0.py
data/studies/**/left_out.csv.gz
# The WTA feed's per-match check results (15 MB), rewritten offline from the raw documents by every refresh
# (src/eda/official_point_feeds/verify_wta.py); its summary, wta_verification.json, stays tracked
data/studies/official_point_feeds/wta_checks.csv

# Every file over 50 MB (50,000,000 bytes) in data/, listed by name, or by folder where a folder holds
# many, so it stays ignored if a rule above is narrowed. GitHub warns above 50 MiB and rejects files
# above 100 MiB. How to regenerate or re-download each one: data/LARGE_FILES.md. Its last section has
# the check (and the fix) for large files git would pick up. Last checked 14 Oct 2026: 187 files, all
# ignored, none tracked. Two folder rules further down belong to this list too:
# data/studies/data_continuity/rebuilds/*/replaced/ and data/studies/current_best_model/*/frozen/.
data/raw/public_dump/atp_pipeline_handoff/
data/raw/public_dump/polymarket_trades/
data/raw/public_dump/polymarket_prices/bodies/itf.jsonl.gz
