# The lower-level feed's first candidate Stage 0s (13 Oct 2026; later weekly ones are built outside the repository,
# in C:/Users/zerom/tnr_feed/candidates/) and the coverage alarm's scratch Stage 0, rebuilt from the raw downloads by
# src/eda/data_gaps_2026/feed.py. The candidates' tables are ignored here and by the type rules (*.parquet,
# left_out.csv.gz). Their small records stay tracked, among them the hand check of 13 Oct (identity_verdicts.csv),
# which exists only there; so do the feed's records (feed/runs.jsonl, coverage/*/summary.json)
data/studies/data_gaps_2026/feed/candidates/*/stage0_match_players.parquet
data/studies/data_gaps_2026/coverage/stage0_scratch/

# Archives and backup bundles anywhere in data/ are never committed, whatever their size. Backups go to
# cold storage (gs://tennis-predictions-archive; see data/LARGE_FILES.md).
data/backups/
# The copies a coordinated Stage 0 rebuild keeps of what it replaced (src/eda/data_continuity/rebuild_stage0.py);
# each rebuild's rebuild.json and id_map.csv stay tracked.
data/studies/data_continuity/rebuilds/*/replaced/
# The frozen reference of the current best model (src/eda/current_best_model/reference.py): its copies stay local and
# reach cold storage with the backups; manifest.json, verify.json, README.md and comparisons/ stay tracked.
data/studies/current_best_model/*/frozen/
data/studies/current_best_model/*/frozen.partial/
data/**/*.zip
data/**/*.7z
data/**/*.tar
data/**/*.tar.gz
data/**/*.tgz

